This code reads the Melexis MLX91219 current sensor through an MCP3008 ADC connected to the Raspberry Pi 5's SPI0 CE0 (spidev0.0) at 1 MHz, mode 0, 8 bits per word, sampling once per second. It logs each reading with an ISO-8601 timestamp to a file named `current_log.txt`. The cooling fan on GPIO18 (BCM) is driven HIGH when the measured current exceeds a defined threshold and LOW otherwise. The program checks the result of every open, ioctl, read, and write call, detects SPI transfer failures, and treats ADC values of all-zero or all-ones as a sensor-absent condition. On receipt of SIGINT or SIGTERM, it closes the SPI file descriptor, releases the GPIO lines, and ensures the fan is turned OFF. The appropriate driver interface for all GPIO control is used, opening the GPIO chip by name and attempting the Pi 5 specific API call before falling back to chip 0.

