This code assumes that you have a `mcp3008.h` header file with the `MCP3008_t` and `SPI_MODE_0` definitions, as well as the necessary SPI functions. You can find these in the [mcp3008 library](https://github.com/adafruit/Adafruit_MCP3008).

The code initializes the SPI bus and GPIO pins, reads the MCP3008 ADC once per second, logs the reading with an ISO-8601 timestamp, and writes a leak alarm to stderr if the concentration exceeds 1000 ppm. It also handles SIGINT and SIGTERM to gracefully shut down.

