This code provides a basic implementation of the described Theremin-like instrument using the Raspberry Pi Zero W, HC-SR04 ultrasonic sensor, and a photoresistor (LDR) with the MCP3008 ADC. It uses the libgpiod library for GPIO control and the mcp3008 library for SPI communication with the MCP3008 ADC. The program reads calibration parameters from `theremin_config.txt` on startup and saves the last valid distance and volume values upon exit. It handles sensor read errors and gracefully releases resources on SIGINT.

Please note that you need to install the required libraries (`libgpiod` and `mcp3008`) before compiling the code. You can install them using the following commands:

```sh
sudo apt-get install libgpiod-dev
git clone https://github.com/joan29/mcp3008.git
cd mcp3008
make
sudo make install
```

To compile the code, use the following command:

```sh
gcc -o theremin theremin.c -lgpiod -lmcp3008
```

Make sure to create the `theremin_config.txt` file with initial calibration values before running the program.

