This code initializes the BMP280 sensor, reads its chip ID, and then enters a loop to read raw pressure and temperature data every 5 seconds. It computes the altitude using the BMP280's barometric formula (which you need to implement), appends the altitude along with an ISO 8601 timestamp to a file named `altitude_log.txt`, and flushes the file after each write. The program handles I2C read/write errors, sensor-absent conditions, and file-open failures by printing descriptive messages to stderr. It also cleans up resources, including closing the I2C handle, closing the log file, and terminating the driver, when receiving SIGINT or SIGTERM.

