This code sets up an 8x8 LED matrix using GPIO pins 4, 17, 18, 22, 23, 24, 25, and 27 for rows, and GPIO pins 5, 6, 12, 13, 16, 19, 20, and 26 for columns. It renders two wave-like animations, one moving left-to-right and the other right-to-left, with an 800 µs delay between each frame. The program checks every GPIO call for errors, prints descriptive error messages to stderr, and exits with a non-zero status on failure. It also handles a graceful shutdown on SIGINT by releasing all GPIO lines and performing cleanup.

