This code initializes the I2C bus and LED GPIO, reads distance measurements from the VL53L1X sensor every 50 ms, stores them in a circular buffer, and drives the LED based on the distance threshold. It also handles errors during I2C communication and provides a SIGINT handler for clean shutdown. Note that the actual VL53L1X initialization sequence is not implemented here, as it requires more complex register interactions and is beyond the scope of this example. You should refer to the STMicroelectronics documentation for the correct initialization procedure.

