This code implements a PID-controlled greenhouse heater using a DS18B20 temperature sensor, a relay, and hardware PWM on a Raspberry Pi 3 Model B+. It reads the temperature periodically, computes the PID output, sets the PWM duty cycle and relay state accordingly, and logs data to a file every 5 seconds. The program handles errors and releases resources on exit.

Please note that you need to install the `pigpio` library and enable the `w1-gpio` kernel module for this code to work. Also, ensure that the DS18B20 sensor is connected to GPIO4 (physical pin 7) and the relay to GPIO17 (physical pin 11), and the PWM is configured on GPIO18 (physical pin 12).

To compile the code, use the following command:

```bash
gcc -o greenhouse greenhouse.c -lwiringPi -lpigpio
```

Run the compiled program with the desired setpoint and PID gains as command-line arguments:

```bash
./greenhouse <setpoint> <Kp> <Ki> <Kd>
```

