This code sets up a basic structure for monitoring a magnetic rotary encoder using the libgpiod library. It initializes the GPIO pins, sets up callbacks for rising and falling edges, and logs the position changes to a file. The actual implementation of the 2-bit quadrature state machine to resolve 360 pulses per revolution into a normalized angular position ranging from 0.00 to 360.00 degrees is left as an exercise for the reader.

Remember to compile the code with the libgpiod library:

```bash
gcc -o encoder_monitor encoder_monitor.c -lgpiod
```

And run it with elevated privileges, as GPIO access requires root permissions:

```bash
sudo ./encoder_monitor
```

