This code sets up a Raspberry Pi 4 Model B to monitor an HC-SR501 PIR sensor connected to GPIO4 and control a door-strike relay connected to GPIO17. It polls the PIR sensor every 50ms, logs motion events, activates the relay for 1 second upon motion detection, and implements a failsafe mechanism for continuous motion detection exceeding 10 seconds. The code uses the libgpiod library for GPIO access and handles errors appropriately. It also sets up signal handlers for SIGINT and SIGTERM to perform a clean shutdown.

