```

This code initializes the GPIO and I2C interfaces, sets up signal handlers for SIGINT and SIGTERM, reads the touch status from the MPR121 capacitive touch controller, debounces touch events, and toggles the relay connected to GPIO17 (BCM) when electrode 0 is touched. It logs all errors with timestamps to the `touch_relay.log` file and handles cleanup on exit or signal reception.

Please note that you need to install the `libgpiod` library and its development headers to compile this code. You can install it using the following command:

```bash
sudo apt-get install libgpiod-dev
```

Compile the code with:

```bash
gcc -o touch_relay touch_relay.c -lgpiod
```

Run the compiled program with:

```bash
sudo ./touch_relay
```

Make sure to connect the MPR121 capacitive touch controller to the I2C bus 1 (SDA to pin 3 and SCL to pin 5) and the relay to GPIO17 (BCM).

