This code initializes the GPIO pins, sets up the interrupt callbacks for rising and falling edges on the ECHO pin, and logs the distance measurements to a file named `distance_log.txt` in CSV format. It handles errors during initialization, file opening, and sensor timeouts. The program runs indefinitely, generating a 10 µs trigger pulse on the TRIG line, waiting 200 ms between trigger cycles, and discarding any measurement whose pulse width exceeds 23,200 µs (approximately 4 m). A SIGINT handler is installed to clean up resources and terminate the program gracefully upon receiving a SIGINT (Ctrl+C).

