This code sets up a line-following robot using a SunFounder 3-Way Tracking Sensor connected to a Raspberry Pi 5. It initializes the GPIO pins, sets up a circular buffer for sensor readings, and polls the sensors every 10 ms. The program handles sensor-absent or bus-error conditions during GPIO initialization and logs readings into the circular buffer. It drives the alert pin HIGH for 2 seconds when the center sensor reports "no line" (logic 1) for five consecutive readings. Otherwise, it moves forward when the center detects a line (logic 0), turns left when the left sensor detects a line, and turns right when the right sensor detects a line. The program stops when all sensors read "no line". On SIGINT or SIGTERM, it cleanly releases all resources.

