This code initializes the MPR121 capacitive touch sensor on I2C bus 1, configures it according to the specified parameters, and toggles a relay connected to GPIO17 on a fresh rising-edge touch of electrode 0 with a 200 ms debounce. It also handles SIGINT and SIGTERM signals for clean exit. Make sure to install the required libraries (`libgpiod` and `libi2c-dev`) before compiling the code.

To compile the code, use the following command:

```bash
gcc -o mpr121_relay mpr121_relay.c -lgpiod -li2c
```

Run the compiled program with:

```bash
sudo ./mpr121_relay
```

Don't forget to connect the MPR121 capacitive touch sensor and the relay to the Raspberry Pi according to the specified GPIO pins.

