This code sets up a Raspberry Pi 3 Model B+ to monitor a TTP223 capacitive touch sensor on GPIO 4 and toggle a 5V relay on GPIO 17 using a stable-level, polling-based debounce of 50ms by default. The debounce interval can be overridden with an optional command-line argument `-d <milliseconds>`. Every relay state change is logged to the console with a timestamp. The program installs SIGINT and SIGTERM handlers that turn the relay OFF, release the driver library resources, and exit cleanly.

