This code initializes the GPIO library, sets up the touch sensor and relay pins, and enters a loop that polls the touch sensor every 50 ms. When the touch sensor is triggered, the relay is toggled. If the touch sensor remains HIGH for more than 10 seconds, the relay is turned OFF, and further toggles are ignored until the sensor is released. The cleanup_flag is set on receiving SIGINT or SIGTERM, and the main loop exits cleanly. Finally, the relay is turned OFF, and the GPIO library is cleaned up.

