This code implements the requested functionality using the `libgpiod` library for GPIO control. It reads the HX711 sensor every 500 ms, enforces a read timeout of 0.5 seconds, and gracefully skips iterations where the timeout occurs. The program initializes the GPIO driver with error checking, loads calibration data from `calibration.txt`, performs a one-time startup calibration by averaging 100 readings at zero load to determine the offset, computes weight using the loaded or default scale and offset, engages the solenoid when the computed weight exceeds a calibrated threshold of 10.0 kg, logs each reading with a timestamp to `weight_log.txt`, and writes any updated calibration values back to `calibration.txt`. The program handles SIGINT to cleanly shut down by releasing all GPIO resources and closing open files.

